{"id": "EUVD-2026-5453", "enisaUuid": "e78519a0-d41f-3970-b601-bb095702a0a4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: usb-audio: Fix use-after-free in snd_usb_mixer_free()\n\nWhen snd_usb_create_mixer() fails, snd_usb_mixer_free() frees\nmixer->id_elems but the controls already added to the card still\nreference the freed memory. Later when snd_card_register() runs,\nthe OSS mixer layer calls their callbacks and hits a use-after-free read.\n\nCall trace:\n  get_ctl_value+0x63f/0x820 sound/usb/mixer.c:411\n  get_min_max_with_quirks.isra.0+0x240/0x1f40 sound/usb/mixer.c:1241\n  mixer_ctl_feature_info+0x26b/0x490 sound/usb/mixer.c:1381\n  snd_mixer_oss_build_test+0x174/0x3a0 sound/core/oss/mixer_oss.c:887\n  ...\n  snd_card_register+0x4ed/0x6d0 sound/core/init.c:923\n  usb_audio_probe+0x5ef/0x2a90 sound/usb/card.c:1025\n\nFix by calling snd_ctl_remove() for all mixer controls before freeing\nid_elems. We save the next pointer first because snd_ctl_remove()\nfrees the current element.", "datePublished": "2026-02-04T16:08:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:25:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51b1aa6fe7dc87356ba58df06afb9677c9b841ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56fb6efd5d04caf6f14994d51ec85393b9a896c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7009daeefa945973a530b2f605fe445fc03747af", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7bff0156d13f0ad9436e5178b979b063d59f572a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6f103a22b08daf5df2f4aa158081840e5910963", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc1a5dd80af1ee1f29d8375b12dd7625f6294dad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/930e69757b74c3ae083b0c3c7419bfe7f0edc7b2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-23089", "GHSA-h8v3-969r-cfp9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "067cb2ef-ef2e-32fe-8c3e-3ca02ce85832", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6639b6c2367f884ca172b78d69f7da17bfab2e5e <dc1a5dd80af1ee1f29d8375b12dd7625f6294dad"}, {"id": "1dd90867-b7f2-3cf3-a0a9-11f50260ab99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6639b6c2367f884ca172b78d69f7da17bfab2e5e <7bff0156d13f0ad9436e5178b979b063d59f572a"}, {"id": "2be9095c-8d7b-3ca3-b6e7-67276c7436b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.13"}, {"id": "36ac590e-0f5d-3e27-be59-0eaf8efad104", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6639b6c2367f884ca172b78d69f7da17bfab2e5e <7009daeefa945973a530b2f605fe445fc03747af"}, {"id": "62577c31-33c1-3fd6-8387-30c2f02b4046", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.199"}, {"id": "6da70573-12ae-3991-82ac-fad49310cfc2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.8"}, {"id": "7150820a-4cbe-3e46-8be2-87841446f0d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6639b6c2367f884ca172b78d69f7da17bfab2e5e <56fb6efd5d04caf6f14994d51ec85393b9a896c6"}, {"id": "7fcb6f1c-7d48-3c48-9b99-94058479c482", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.122"}, {"id": "90da2003-fb43-3513-b215-ad868c060feb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6639b6c2367f884ca172b78d69f7da17bfab2e5e <51b1aa6fe7dc87356ba58df06afb9677c9b841ea"}, {"id": "95958d84-4dcd-35d8-9848-9bb214c5412b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.249"}, {"id": "b6733368-4f40-30fa-83bf-11c06679e541", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6639b6c2367f884ca172b78d69f7da17bfab2e5e <e6f103a22b08daf5df2f4aa158081840e5910963"}, {"id": "c9fa99dd-bc54-392b-be19-6ca7a57c0e43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19"}, {"id": "ce3a8285-e363-3314-8d96-d27e95a2a618", "product": {"name": "Lin